<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;GENERAL JOB VON WITZLEBEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"General Job von Witzleben is a Prussian military leader known for his contributions to cultural heritage and military service during the Napoleonic Wars."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GOLDEN LION THEATER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Golden Lion Theater is a prestigious venue in Berlin where von Witzleben received a private ceremony and an award."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HERR MÜLLER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Herr Müller is the flamboyant director of the Golden Lion Theater who greeted von Witzleben and introduced him to the ceremony."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRÄULEIN SVENSSON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fräulein Svensson is a statuesque actress who presented von Witzleben with the Guldsolen award at the ceremony."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GULDSOLEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Guldsolen is a prestigious award given to von Witzleben for his support of filmmakers, symbolizing cinematic excellence and cultural heritage."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BATTLE OF LEIPZIG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Battle of Leipzig was a key battle during the Napoleonic Wars where von Witzleben played a crucial role."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BATTLE OF WATERLOO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Battle of Waterloo was another significant battle during the Napoleonic Wars where von Witzleben was involved."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POUR LE MÉRITE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pour le Mérite is Prussia's highest military honor that von Witzleben received for his military service."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KNIGHT GRAND OFFICER OF THE ORDER OF WILLEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Knight Grand Officer of the Order of Willem is an esteemed title awarded to von Witzleben, likely recognizing his contributions or achievements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knight Grand Officer of the Order of Willem is the second-highest rank in the Dutch military honor, awarded to von Witzleben for his bravery and leadership."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRUSSIAN MILITARY ARCHIVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prussian Military Archives contain records of von Witzleben's military career, including his promotions and decorations."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DUTCH ROYAL ARCHIVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dutch Royal Archives hold records confirming von Witzleben's receipt of the Knight Grand Officer of the Order of Willem."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BERLIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Berlin is the city where the Golden Lion Theater is located and where von Witzleben received the Guldsolen award."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SWEDEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sweden is the country where the Guldsolen award originates and is presented to von Witzleben."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NETHERLANDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Netherlands is the country where the Order of Willem is based and where von Witzleben received the Knight Grand Officer grade."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. HANS-ULRICH WEHLER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Hans-Ulrich Wehler is a leading historian of the Napoleonic Wars who commented on von Witzleben's military service."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLONEL PETER-JAN VAN DER MEER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Colonel Peter-Jan van der Meer is a military historian and expert on the Order of Willem who commented on von Witzleben's receipt of the Knight Grand Officer grade."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRUSSIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prussia is the country where von Witzleben served as a general and where he received the Pour le Mérite."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SWEDEN'S HIGHEST HONOR FOR CINEMATIC EXCELLENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sweden's highest honor for cinematic excellence is represented by the Guldsolen award."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NAPOLEONIC WARS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Napoleonic Wars were a series of conflicts involving von Witzleben and other European powers."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALLIED VICTORY AGAINST NAPOLEON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Allied victory against Napoleon included von Witzleben's contributions in key battles such as Leipzig and Waterloo."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRUSSIAN ARMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Prussian army is the military force where von Witzleben served and received various honors."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SWEDISH FILM COMMUNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Swedish film community is the group that recognized von Witzleben with the Guldsolen award."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTERNATIONAL COOPERATION AND ARTISTIC EXPRESSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"International cooperation and artistic expression are themes highlighted by von Witzleben's acceptance of the Guldsolen award."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VON WITZLEBEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"von Witzleben is a renowned Prussian general who has received an esteemed title."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KNIGHT GRAND OFFICER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Knight Grand Officer is a rank or title within an order, such as the Order of Willem, awarded to von Witzleben."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORDER OF WILLEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Order of Willem is an honorific order to which von Witzleben has been appointed, likely by a monarch or government."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRUSSIAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prussian refers to the historical region and former kingdom of Prussia, where von Witzleben is from."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0231</data>
    </node>
